  "validation_domain": "Six independent normal native cases: exact Preset base C2 and Fx C1/C2, each null/non-null front selection (base has same normal provider state). Native base C2 executes inside both Fx bodies. Host compares exact decoded 336-byte ParamInfo table fields, real CCL parameter classes/current/default/reset/formatter, name/display, SAME service identity, empty delta5 recalls/current child, stable delegate and optional observer membership/order. Actual C++ failure sweep and deletion prove zero outstanding tracked allocations and detached observer at every throwing allocation point. Fresh 24-case existing D0/D1/D2 native/provider lifecycle replay preserves earlier bounded coverage without new credit.",
  "limitations": [
    "Intentional portable composition reuses actual canonical PresetComponent lifecycle. No original inheritance, ARM layout/vtables/calling convention or hardware interoperability claim. Native Fx C1 and C2 call exact base C2; host composition uses actual PresetComponent construction (host C1/C2 alias emitted). Base C1 is not a target or new readiness credit.",
    "Normal original constructor instruction paths executed offline with all exact ranges checked separately. Core calls use explicit typed boundaries; native Core implementation, ARM exception landing pads/unwinder and allocator are not executed. Native failure-path equivalence is not claimed.",
    "Real SAME PresetApplicationServices is a mandatory borrowed binding, not a fabricated production provider. Services/front parameter owner outlive Fx. Service internals and opaque stable delegate token retain explicit source-port boundaries. Original delegate adjustment and Fx observer dispatch remain outside this initialization/lifecycle domain.",
    "Host exception safety is intentional source-port adaptation. Pinned CCL ParamList::add(ParamInfo) leaks its freshly constructed raw parameter if backing vector growth throws. Application constructor uses actual CCL NumericParam/StringParam guarded by unique_ptr until actual ParamList ownership transfer. Vendor untouched; host failure sweep proves cleanup, not native failure equivalence.",
    "Native display is exact My Fx (lowercase x). Sealed TASK/contract My FX spelling was mistaken. Root confirmed correction; sealed historical packet unchanged. Source follows observed ELF string, not task spelling.",
    "Test-only -fno-access-control permits reading actual provider parameter metadata/observer membership; no replacement Core class/provider exists. Global operator new/delete interposition is private to standalone test binary. Canonical CTest executable must retain assertions and this test compile option.",
    "Allocation failure sweep is finite (each throwing new/new[] position through first successful construction) and single threaded. CCL removeObserver retains external parameter observer capacity; test frees that provider-owned reusable storage after membership reaches zero, before outstanding-allocation assertions. Host null-return allocation failures, asynchronous callbacks, concurrent state, file/network/hardware and other provider-internal semantics are excluded. Existing destructor replay is resealed without new destructor reconstruction credit.",
    "No ready/pending admission fragments produced; Root owns canonical full Linux integration, production partition/public headers, installed-role/compile-once, fresh active proof, guarded SQLite dry-run/admission, tracker and mirror gates."
  ],
